{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Exporting and Checking a Tracking Plan","role":"article"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingplanworkflow"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Export the JSON Schema of every event an app tracks, commit it, and fail the build when the events stop matching it."}],"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents"],"generated":true,"title":"Guides"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The events’ Swift types are the source of their schema. A tracking plan, the JSON Schema (draft"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"2020-12) of every event an app tracks, is exported from them for the people and tools outside the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"app. "},{"code":"TrackingPlan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", a product of its own that "},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"leaves out) turns schemas into the plan’s files, one document per event and an index, as values:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import TrackingPlans","","let plan = TrackingPlan(schemas: [CheckoutStarted.schema])","let paths = plan.files.map(\\.path)","\/\/ [\"tracking-plan.json\", \"checkout_started.v2.schema.json\", \"checkout_started.v2.example.json\"]"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The bytes depend on the schemas alone: keys sorted, two-space indentation, a trailing newline and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no timestamps, the same on every run and platform, so the plan can be committed and reviewed.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"What-each-document-says","type":"heading","text":"What each document says","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each document requires the properties that are neither optional nor have a default value, allows","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for the optional ones, and rejects any other property. It carries the event’s version and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"consent category (","type":"text"},{"code":"x-traffluent-version","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"x-traffluent-consent-category","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). A ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"property is marked ","type":"text"},{"code":"x-traffluent-sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and one with a default value is marked","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"x-traffluent-default","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and isn’t required, since an earlier release’s payload lacks it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A property removed at the same version stays in the document with the schema it had, marked"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deprecated"},{"type":"text","text":" and not required, so the payloads of releases that still send it validate: exporting"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"over the committed plan carries it forward. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"type":"text","text":"’s documentation lists how each Swift"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type maps."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Beside each document is the event’s example, a conformance vector: the payload with every property","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"set to a fixed value its schema accepts (","type":"text"},{"code":"\"example\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", 0, ","type":"text"},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", one array element). Another","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"platform’s client can encode the same event and compare it against the example.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Exporting-the-plan","type":"heading","text":"Exporting the plan","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A tool can only read the schemas of types it is compiled against, so the plan is written by a small","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"executable in your package that lists your events:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["\/\/ Package.swift",".executableTarget(name: \"AppTrackingPlan\", dependencies: [","    \"AppEvents\",","    .product(name: \"TrackingPlans\", package: \"Traffluent\"),","]),"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The example package’s executable, ","type":"text"},{"code":"StoreTrackingPlan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", is one:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import StoreEvents","import TrackingPlans","","\/\/\/ Writes the store's tracking plan: `swift package --allow-writing-to-package-directory","\/\/\/ export-tracking-plan`, from Examples\/, writes it into Examples\/TrackingPlan.","@main","struct StoreTrackingPlan: TrackingPlanCommand {","    static let trackingPlan = TrackingPlan(schemas: [","        CheckoutStarted.schema,","        OrderCompleted.schema,","        SignedUp.schema,","    ])","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Then one command, run from the package’s directory, builds it and writes the plan into","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan\/"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["swift package --allow-writing-to-package-directory export-tracking-plan"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"sh"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"export-tracking-plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plugin runs the package’s one executable target that depends on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"code":"--product <name>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" picks one of several, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"--output <directory>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" writes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"elsewhere in the package. Writing again deletes the documents of events the plan no longer lists.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/tree\/main\/Examples\/TrackingPlan","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is the plan ","type":"text"},{"code":"StoreTrackingPlan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" writes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Checking-the-plan","type":"heading","text":"Checking the plan","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The committed plan is the contract every platform that sends the events agrees on. One command"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fails when the Swift events no longer match it, with a line naming each event and property that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"changed:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["swift package check-tracking-plan"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"sh"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A difference is breaking when, at the same version, a record a store still holds or a payload an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"already released app sends may stop decoding or validating:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"a removed or renamed event;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"a retyped property;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"an optional property made required;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"a new required property without a default value;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"a default value removed;"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"a deprecated property declared again with another type, or as required."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Anything else leaves the committed plan out of date, which fails with its own message telling you to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"export it again: a new event, a new optional property or one with a default value, a removed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property, a deprecated one declared again as it was, or a changed consent category."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A constraint is compared keyword by keyword. Tightening one is breaking: a higher ","type":"text"},{"code":"minLength","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"minimum","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a lower ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxLength","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"maximum","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a new bound, a new or changed ","type":"text"},{"code":"pattern","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Loosening one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only leaves the plan out of date. An integer type narrowed to one of fewer bits tightens its bounds","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the same way. Raising an event’s version (","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event(version: 3)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") is how a breaking change is made on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"purpose: the new version gets a document of its own. ","type":"text"},{"code":"--plan <directory>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" checks a plan committed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"elsewhere, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"--product <name>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" picks the executable, as it does for export.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Checking-from-a-test","type":"heading","text":"Checking from a test","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The same check runs from a test, so it runs wherever the app’s tests do. Add the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" product to a test target that depends on the executable, as the example","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"package’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"StoreTrackingPlanTests","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import Foundation","@testable import StoreTrackingPlan","import Testing","import TrackingPlanTesting","","@Suite(\"StoreTrackingPlan\")","struct StoreTrackingPlanTests {","    @Test(\"The store's events match its committed tracking plan\")","    func eventsMatchTheTrackingPlan() {","        let plan = URL(fileURLWithPath: #filePath)","            .deletingLastPathComponent().deletingLastPathComponent().deletingLastPathComponent()","            .appendingPathComponent(\"TrackingPlan\")","        expectTrackingPlan(StoreTrackingPlan.trackingPlan, matches: plan)","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It records an issue with the report the command prints. ","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackingPlan.check(against:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" returns the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"same comparison as a value, each ","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackingPlanDifference","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with whether it ","type":"text"},{"code":"isBreaking","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://TrackingPlans/documentation/TrackingPlans":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","type":"topic","abstract":[],"title":"TrackingPlans","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/trackingplans","role":"collection"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","title":"Traffluent","abstract":[{"text":"Vendor-neutral analytics for Swift: typed events, tracked by a tracker and delivered in batches to any number of destinations.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent","role":"collection"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/AutomaticTracking":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Track screen views, control activations and the app’s lifecycle without a call at each place they happen."}],"title":"Automatic Tracking","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/automatictracking","role":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/PersistingRecords":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","type":"topic","title":"Persisting Records","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so a record the app tracked survives the process ending."}],"role":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/DefiningEvents":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Derive an event’s conformances and schema from its declaration with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and constrain which values its properties may hold.","type":"text"}],"title":"Defining Events","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/definingevents","role":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ConsentGating":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Deliver an event only once the user grants the purpose it is collected for."}],"title":"Consent Gating","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/consentgating","role":"article"},"https://github.com/Tyler-Keith-Thompson/Traffluent/tree/main/Examples/TrackingPlan":{"titleInlineContent":[{"code":"Examples\/TrackingPlan","type":"codeVoice"}],"title":"Examples\/TrackingPlan","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/tree\/main\/Examples\/TrackingPlan","type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/tree\/main\/Examples\/TrackingPlan"},"doc://TrackingPlanTesting/documentation/TrackingPlanTesting":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting","type":"topic","abstract":[],"title":"TrackingPlanTesting","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/trackingplantesting","role":"collection"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SessionsAndStandardContext":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Stamp every event with its session and with the app, device, system, locale and network it was tracked on."}],"title":"Sessions and Standard Context","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/sessionsandstandardcontext","role":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SamplingEvents":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep a seeded fraction of the events a tracker tracks, event by event or a whole session at once."}],"title":"Sampling Events","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/samplingevents","role":"article"}}}